s.md:35:- `plugin_enabled` is keyed by plugin id, not by plugin spec.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:36:- For file plugins, that id must come from the plugin module's exported `id`. For npm plugins, it is the exported `id` or the package name if `id` is omitted.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:37:- Plugins are enabled by default. `plugin_enabled` is only for explicit overrides, usually to disable a plugin with `false`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:38:- `plugin_enabled` is merged across config layers.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:39:- Runtime enable/disable state is also stored in KV under `plugin_enabled`; that KV state overrides config on startup.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:45:- Import types from `@opencode-ai/plugin/tui`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:46:- `@opencode-ai/plugin` exports `./tui` and declares optional peer deps on `@opentui/core` and `@opentui/solid`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:52:import type { TuiPlugin, TuiPluginModule } from \"@opencode-ai/plugin/tui\"\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:55:  api.command.register(() => [\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:75:const plugin: TuiPluginModule & { id: string } = {\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:80:export default plugin\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:90:- `package.json` `main` is only used for server plugin entrypoint resolution.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:92:- File/path plugins must export a non-empty `id`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:93:- npm plugins may omit `id`; package `name` is used.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:94:- Runtime identity is the resolved plugin id. Later plugins with the same id are rejected, including collisions with internal plugin ids.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:97:- Legacy compatibility: path specs like `./plugin` can resolve to `./plugin/index.ts` (or `index.js`) when `package.json` is missing.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.m