packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:33:- Duplicate npm plugins are deduped by package name; higher-precedence config wins.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:34:- Duplicate file plugins are deduped by exact resolved file spec. This happens while merging config, before plugin modules are loaded.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:35:- `plugin_enabled` is keyed by plugin id, not by plugin spec.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:36:- For file plugins, that id must come from the plugin module's exported `id`. For npm plugins, it is the exported `id` or the package name if `id` is omitted.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:37:- Plugins are enabled by default. `plugin_enabled` is only for explicit overrides, usually to disable a plugin with `false`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:38:- `plugin_enabled` is merged across config layers.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:39:- Runtime enable/disable state is also stored in KV under `plugin_enabled`; that KV state overrides config on startup.
