packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:190:`api.command.register` returns an unregister function. Command rows support:
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:203:- Hidden commands are removed from the command dialog and slash list, but still respond to keybinds and `command.trigger(value)` if `enabled !== false`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:208:- Any other name is treated as a plugin route.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:214:- If multiple plugins register the same route name, the last registered route wins.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:215:- Unknown plugin routes render a fallback screen with a `go home` action.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:232:- `api.keybind.create(defaults, overrides?)` builds a plugin-local keybind set.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:238:- `api.kv` is the shared app KV store backed by `state/kv.json`. It is not plugin-namespaced.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:253:  - `session.permission(sessionID)`
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:276:- Relative theme paths are resolved from the plugin root.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:279:- If the theme name already exists, install is skipped unless plugin metadata state is `updated`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:280:- On `updated`, host only rewrites themes previously tracked for that plugin and only when source `mtime`/`size` changed.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:281:- Local plugins persist installed themes under the local `.opencode/themes` area near the plugin config source.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:282:- Global plugins persist installed themes under the global `themes` dir.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:300:- `api.slots.register(plugin)` returns the host-assigned slot plugin id.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:301:- `api.slots.register(plugin)` does not return an unregister function.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:302:- Returned ids are `pluginId`, `pluginId:1`, `pluginId:2`, and so on.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:309:- `api.plugins.list()` returns `{ id, source, spec, target, enabled, active }[]`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:310:- `enabled` is the persisted desired state. `active` means the plugin is currently initialized.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:311:- `api.plugins.activate(id)` sets `enabled=true`, persists it into KV, and initializes the plugin.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:312:- `api.plugins.deactivate(id)` sets `enabled=false`, persists it into KV, and disposes the plugin scope.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:313:- `api.plugins.add(spec)` trims the input and returns `false` for an empty string.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:314:- `api.plugins.add(spec)` treats the input as the runtime plugin spec and loads it without re-reading `tui.json`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:315:- `api.plugins.add(spec)` no-ops when that resolved spec (or resolved plugin id) is already loaded.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:316:- `api.plugins.add(spec)` assumes enabled and always attempts initialization (it does not consult config/KV enable state).
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:317:- `api.plugins.install(spec, { global? })` runs install -> manifest read -> config patch using the same helper flow as CLI install.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:318:- `api.plugins.install(...)` returns either `{ ok: false, message, missing? }` or `{ ok: true, dir, tui }`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:319:- `api.plugins.install(...)` does not load plugins into the current session. Call `api.plugins.add(spec)` to load after install.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:320:- For packages that declare a tuple `tui` target in `oc-plugin`, `api.plugins.install(...)` stages those tuple options so a following `api.plugins.add(spec)` uses them.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:321:- If activation fails, the plugin can remain `enabled=true` and `active=false`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:335:Metadata is persisted by plugin id.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:337:- File plugin fingerprint is `target|modified`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:338:- npm plugin fingerprint is `target|requested|version`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:339:- Internal plugins get synthetic metadata with `state: "same"`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:343:- Internal TUI plugins load first.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:344:- External TUI plugins load from `tuiConfig.plugin`.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:345:- `--pure` / `OPENCODE_PURE` skips external TUI plugins only.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:346:- External plugin resolution and import are parallel.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:347:- External plugin activation is sequential to keep command, route, and side-effect order deterministic.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:348:- File plugins that fail initially are retried once after waiting for config dependency installation.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:349:- Runtime add uses the same external loader path, including the file-plugin retry after dependency wait.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:352:- Plugin init failure rolls back that plugin's tracked registrations and loading continues.
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:354:  - command registrations
packages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:361:- Total cleanup budget per plugin is 5 seconds; timeout/error is logged and shutdown continues.
